    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Why this story matters now.</h2>
      <p class="dropcap">For half a century a breakaway faction of the Catholic Church has operated in the seams of Western institutions, outside the authority of Rome and off the radar of the press. The Society of St. Pius X has produced a Holocaust-denying bishop expelled by his own order, a flagship boarding school whose alumni include a Republic of Texas militiaman, and a chapel that hosted Timothy McVeigh four days before Oklahoma City. On July 1, 2026, it consecrated four bishops without a papal mandate. On July 2, Pope Leo XIV declared the Society in schism.</p>
      <p>Lou Massett was raised inside all of it. He went to school with one of the four new bishops. <em>Traddyland</em> is the first book to tell that story from the inside.</p>
      <p>The world of the book is specific. The pattern it traces is not. If you have ever watched someone you love disappear into an ideology, or felt that pull yourself, this story will feel familiar.</p>
      <a class="textlink" href="/book/">About the book →</a>
