      <h2>A writer working from inside the world he is trying to understand.</h2>
      <p class="lede">Lou Massett was raised in the Society of St. Pius X and spent five years at its boarding school in Kansas. He left the movement in his early twenties and spent the next thirty years working out what had happened. <em>Traddyland</em> is his first book.</p>
      <p>In July 2026 Newsweek quoted him on the human cost of the excommunications. His essay on St. Marys ran in UnHerd the same month.</p>
